// @emit-error ref valtype with no interned shape
// A FLOOR PIN, not a decision — flip it when the floor lifts. A verdict pin rather than a
// `@log` one because the program never lowers, so no correct output exists to observe.
//
// A module GLOBAL annotated with a union-VARIANT type name. `types/variant-as-value.vl` pins
// a variant type as a first-class value in every OTHER position — local, param, return,
// argument, array element — so this is the one position that pin does not reach, and the gap
// is the position, not the feature.
//
// THE MECHANISM: `buildLocals` has a `variant` rung (`letIsVariant` → kind 8, the bare variant
// struct ref) ahead of its `letIsUnion`/`letIsStruct` rungs. `globalCellKind`, whose own header
// says it mirrors that ladder, has no such rung — so the annotation falls to `letIsStruct`,
// `globalCellStructIdx` asks `structIndexOfLet`, and a variant's `TypeDecl` is deliberately
// absent from the struct table (`collectS` skips it; the variant table owns it). Index -1 then
// trips `fbValtypeNullable`'s out-of-bounds guard, which is where this message comes from.
//
// MEASURED, each cell its own program:
//   - the identical binding as a LOCAL inside a function lowers and prints — STORAGE CLASS IS
//     THE AXIS for this cell;
//   - as a function PARAM it lowers;
//   - a struct|struct union (`Outer | Other`) floors exactly as this struct|scalar one does,
//     so union MIXEDNESS is not the axis;
//   - a NESTED field (`{p: Inner}`) as a local lowers, so nesting is not the axis either;
//   - un-annotate the binding and the message CHANGES to `field access but no struct type
//     declared` — a separate floor with a separate root
//     (`variant-fieldset-twin-anon-shape-floor.vl`).
//
// Lifting this means teaching the GLOBAL cell ladder the `variant` rep — `globalCellKind`,
// a variant-index resolver beside `globalCellStructIdx`, and a `pendingVariantIdx` seed at the
// global initializer, against 33 `globalCellKind` call sites. That is a rep slice, and no
// corpus row exercises it today, so it is pinned here rather than guessed at.
type Outer = { p: i32 }
type U = Outer | i32

const g: Outer = { p: 5 }
print(g.p)
